    "result": "I fixed the bug, but I haven't run any checks. The `tests` directory isn't in this checkout, so I couldn't run the suite. My inline Python sanity check was blocked by a permission prompt.\n\nThe bug was in `_handle_closing_keyword` in `sqlparse/engine/statement_splitter.py`. The `END IF` branch had an inverted condition (`if not (...)`), so it popped the block stack when the top wasn't an `IF`. I removed the `not`, so it now pops only when the top of the stack is `IF`.\n\nThat should restore correct splitting for the `issue194` function case and the `endifloop` parse case. I'm inferring that from the code, not from a passing test."
